<title>USA: 1st Source sets five-for-four stock split.</title>
<headline>1st Source sets five-for-four stock split.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTH BEND, Ind. 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>1st Source Inc said Tuesday its board of directors approved a five-for-four stock split.</p>
<p>1st Source said the split will be payable on February 14 to shareholders of record on February 5.  </p>
<p>1st Source, the parent company of 1st Source Bank, also set a quarterly cash dividend of $0.09 a share, the same as the previous quarter's dividend but up 18.1 percent from the fourth quarter last year.</p>
<p>The dividend will also be payable on February 14 to shareholders of record on February 5.  The company said the cash dividend will apply to shares held prior to the stock split.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
